\title{conductoR: perform a contract-typed analytical plan}
\description{
A plan (\link{oap_plan}) is a directed acyclic graph of nodes (\code{\link[=node]{node()}}), each
bound to a tool that returns an \link[orchestraManifest:orchestra_manifest]{orchestraManifest::orchestra_manifest}.
\code{\link[=conduct]{conduct()}} performs it in topological order and refuses any handoff whose
declared inferential target does not match what the upstream node emitted.
Two operators are built in: an abstention gate that will not pass a null
verdict the design could not have resolved, and a triangulation that
reconciles any number of lenses on one question. A plan round-trips through
YAML (\code{\link[=plan_to_yaml]{plan_to_yaml()}}, \code{\link[=plan_from_yaml]{plan_from_yaml()}}) and compiles to a 'targets'
pipeline (\code{\link[=compile_to_targets]{compile_to_targets()}}).
